# Rank 1550 / CVE-2020-35910: parking_lot's lock guards carried
# unsafe Send/Sync impls with bounds too weak for the data they
# expose, so a guard over non-Send data could cross threads and race
# on its target (thread-safety soundness hole, CWE-662/CWE-362; PR
# #262 "Fix bounds on Send and Sync impls for lock guards"). The
# impls in src/lock_api.rs read `unsafe impl<'a, R: RawRwLock + 'a,
# T: ?Sized + Sync + 'a> Sync for RwLockReadGuard<'a, R, T> {}` and
# -- decisively -- `unsafe impl<'a, R: RawRwLock + 'a, T: ?Sized +
# 'a> Send for MappedRwLockReadGuard<'a, R, T>` with NO T bound at
# all: moving the guard to another thread moves its reference to T
# with it, whatever T is. the fixing commit is the fixing change
# (confirmed, the guard_sync merge): every Send impl now requires
# `T: ?Sized + Send`, the read/write guards' Sync impls sit behind
# the right bounds, and a GuardNoSend marker opt-out is added.

#
# ATTENTION, unsafe impl bounds. The defect lives in trait-safety
# declarations -- which generic bounds make an unsafe impl sound is
# Rust type-system semantics no observation models: the corpus's
# concurrency rules judge dataflow races (VYQL-RACE-002
# LocklessSharedMutation, RACE-001 FileToctou), not the correctness
# of unsafe impl declarations. A binding on parking_lot's own guards
# would detect this crate rather than the weakness. Measured on the
# real code: scanning src/ reports the same 55 findings at both
# revisions (13 rust files; none change with the bounds). No
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: unsafe-impl bound checking is language
# semantics, not a localised construct. No definition change
# shipped. Spec cve_rank1550 records the unbounded Send impl and the
# T: Send-bounded form, both asserting reject VYQL-RACE-002: when
# unsafe-impl vocabulary lands, the unbounded form must flip to
# expect.

test "rank1550: the mapped guard sends whatever it wraps"
  lang rust
  file src/lock_api.rs
  reject VYQL-RACE-002
  code
  ```
  use crate::raw_rwlock::RawRwLock;

  pub struct MappedRwLockReadGuard<'a, R: RawRwLock, T: ?Sized> {
      raw: &'a R,
      data: *const T,
  }

  unsafe impl<'a, R: RawRwLock + 'a, T: ?Sized + 'a> Send
      for MappedRwLockReadGuard<'a, R, T>
  where
      R::GuardMarker: Send,
  {
  }
  ```

test "rank1550: the fixed revision bounds send on the wrapped data"
  lang rust
  file src/lock_api.rs
  reject VYQL-RACE-002
  code
  ```
  use crate::raw_rwlock::RawRwLock;

  pub struct MappedRwLockReadGuard<'a, R: RawRwLock, T: ?Sized> {
      raw: &'a R,
      data: *const T,
  }

  unsafe impl<'a, R: RawRwLock + 'a, T: ?Sized + Sync + 'a> Send
      for MappedRwLockReadGuard<'a, R, T>
  where
      R::GuardMarker: Send,
  {
  }
  ```
